  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "name": "ELM benchmark for PV prediction",
  "description": "A benchmark of simple statistical models for photovoltaic power forecasting (AC output, after the inverter) across horizons from 30 minutes to 10 hours ahead. Compares persistence baselines, convex BLEND combinations, a linear AR-OLS model, and a family of Extreme Learning Machine variants differing in loss function and regularization, together with foundation-model and NeuralProphet references. Models are evaluated with NICE, the ratio of their error to that of simple persistence at the same horizon, on several PV sites.",
